<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP MEDAL ROUND RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP MEDAL ROUND RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the medal round at</p>
<p>the ice hockey world championships on Wednesday:</p>
<p>Czech Republic 5 Canada 3 (2-2 1-0 2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Czech Republic - Vladimir Vujtek (07:00, 28:55, 40:57),</p>
<p>Martin Prochazka (08:38), Rostislav Vlach (48:29)</p>
<p>Canada - Rob Zamuner (02:34, 14:01), Don Sweeney (50:41)</p>
<p>Penalties: Canada 122 minutes, Czech Republic 122</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,111</p>
<p>Sweden 5 Finland 2 (2-0 2-2 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sweden - Jonas Hoglund (05:30), Per Eklund (11:11), Michael</p>
<p>Nylander (35:04), Jorgen Jonsson (38:31), Nichlas Falk (43:53).</p>
<p>Finland - Ville Peltonen (27:59, 33:50).</p>
<p>Penalties: Sweden 24 minutes, Finland 18</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,328</p>
<p>    Standings	  P   W  D  L   F  A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Sweden	     4   3  0  1  16   9    6</p>
<p> 2. Russia	     4   2  1  1  12  11    5</p>
<p> 3. Czech Republic   4   2  0  2  12  11    4</p>
<p> 4. Canada	     4   2  0  2  11  13    4</p>
<p> 5. United States    4   1  1  2   7  12    3</p>
<p> 6. Finland	    4   1  0  3  10  12    2</p>
<p>Remaining matches: Czech Republic v Sweden (Thursday),</p>
<p>Canada v Russia, United States v Finland (Friday).</p>
